2. The following non‑citizens (other than a non‑citizen who holds a valid passport from a country that is approved by the Minister under section 9B(2) of the Act) are exempt from section 9B(1) of the Act:
(a)a permanent resident of Singapore;
(b)any head of state of a foreign country who is a guest of the Government;
(c)a non‑citizen who holds a valid laissez‑passer issued by the United Nations;
(d)a member of any visiting force within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Visiting Forces Act 1960;
(e)a crew member of an aircraft that arrives in Singapore from a place outside Singapore (whether in a journey to Singapore, or in the course of a journey from a place outside Singapore to another place outside Singapore);
(f)a non‑citizen (excluding a non‑citizen holding a pass that entitles him or her to enter Singapore multiple times) who holds a valid ordinary passport issued by the government of the People’s Republic of China;
(g)a non‑citizen who is —
(i)duly accredited to Singapore as a diplomatic or consular representative of the government of the Republic of Poland, and holds a valid diplomatic passport, official passport, service passport or public affairs passport issued by the government of that country;
(ii)a staff member of any diplomatic or consular representative of the government of the Republic of Poland, and holds a valid diplomatic passport, official passport, service passport or public affairs passport issued by the government of that country; or
(iii)a spouse or dependent child of a person mentioned in sub‑paragraph (i) or (ii);
(h)a non‑citizen who holds a valid passport that is issued by the government of any foreign country specified in the Schedule, the passport being of the type specified opposite that country;
(i)a non‑citizen arriving in Singapore in special circumstances where an emergency has affected the non‑citizen’s ability to apply for a Singapore visa.
